 \section{Related Work}
 \subsection{Minimum-Cost Reach-Avoid Learning}
-In reach-avoid reinforcement learning, reaching a target and avoiding an unsafe
-set are treated as trajectory-level requirements rather than competing reward terms
-\cite{bansal2017,hsu2021}. This formulation is extended to minimum-cost
-reach-avoid control in RC-PPO through state augmentation with a safety indicator
-and remaining budget, budget-conditioned policy and reachability-critic learning,
-and a search for the least feasible initial budget~\cite{so2024}. This formulation
-is adopted as the algorithmic foundation for connecting nominal MCRA decisions
-to quadruped execution.
+Reach-avoid reinforcement learning treats target reaching and unsafe-set
+avoidance as trajectory-level requirements rather than competing reward
+terms~\cite{bansal2017,hsu2021}. RC-PPO extends this to MCRA through safety/budget
+state augmentation, budget-conditioned policy and reachability-critic learning,
+and least-feasible-budget search~\cite{so2024}. We adopt this foundation to
+connect nominal MCRA decisions to quadruped execution.
 
